# Flutter Widget Best Practices

## Composition

- Prefer composing small widgets over extending existing ones.
- Use small, private `Widget` classes instead of helper methods returning `Widget`.
- Break large `build()` methods into smaller private widget classes — not private methods.

```dart
// ✅ Private widget class
class _Header extends StatelessWidget {
  const _Header({required this.title});
  final String title;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Text(title, style: ...);
}

// ❌ Helper method returning widget
Widget _buildHeader(String title) => Text(title, style: ...);
```

## Performance

- Use `const` constructors for widgets and in `build()` wherever possible.
- Never perform expensive operations (network calls, heavy computation) inside `build()`.
- Use `ListView.builder` or `SliverList` for long or dynamic lists — never `ListView` with `children`.
- Use `compute()` for expensive work (e.g., JSON parsing) to avoid blocking the UI thread.

## Layout Primitives

- **`Expanded`:** Fill remaining space along the main axis in a `Row`/`Column`.
- **`Flexible`:** Allow a widget to shrink-to-fit, but not necessarily expand.
- **`Wrap`:** Use when items may overflow a `Row`/`Column` and need to wrap to the next line.
- **`SingleChildScrollView`:** For fixed-size content that may overflow the viewport.
- **`FittedBox`:** Scale/fit a single child within its parent constraints.
- **`LayoutBuilder`:** Make layout decisions based on available constraints.

## Responsive Design

- Use `LayoutBuilder` or `MediaQuery` for responsive layouts.
- Use `Theme.of(context).textTheme` for text styles — never hardcode font sizes.

## Overlays

- Use `OverlayPortal` (with `OverlayPortalController`) for custom dropdowns or tooltips that render on top of everything else.
- Use `Positioned` to anchor children within a `Stack` by edge offsets.
- Use `Align` to position children within a `Stack` using alignment values.

## Immutability

- `StatelessWidget` must be fully immutable — all fields `final`.
- When UI needs to change, Flutter rebuilds the widget tree; do not mutate widget fields.
